  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{\u2032}(t)=\u27e8\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,,4{e}^{-2t}\u27e9\n$$\n\n and $F(1)=\u27e811,\\,-2{e}^{-2}+3\u27e9.$\n\n$F(t)=\u27e8${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$\u27e9$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{\u2032}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \u27e8\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,,4{e}^{-2t}\u27e9\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \u27e8\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,,4{e}^{-2t}\u27e9\\text{d}t & =\u27e8\\int \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int 4{e}^{-2t}\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e86\\sqrt{t}+{c}_{1},\\,-2{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=\u27e811,\\,-2{e}^{-2}+3\u27e9$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=\u27e86\\sqrt{1}+{c}_{1},\\,-2{e}^{-2}+{c}_{2}\u27e9 & =\u27e811,\\,-2{e}^{-2}+3\u27e9 \\\\ \u27e86+{c}_{1},\\,-2{e}^{-2}+{c}_{2}\u27e9 & =\u27e811,\\,-2{e}^{-2}+3\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=5$ and ${c}_{2}=3.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=\u27e86\\sqrt{t}+5,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}+3\u27e9.\n$$",
